            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "The line and parabola do not meet.",
              "worked": "There is no point satisfying both equations, so the line and parabola do not intersect.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suppose Bob is given a line that is tangential to a parabola. Solving their equations simultaneously produces a quadratic equation. How many distinct roots should he expect this quadratic equation to have?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "One distinct root, which is a repeated root.",
          "worked": "A tangent meets the parabola at one point. The resulting quadratic equation therefore has one distinct real root, occurring twice.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
